5,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Good morning, everyone. To ensure this park doesn't just look splendid on paper but actually lasts, I believe we should prioritize the long-term durability of the city's execution over mere aesthetic promises. Shall we begin?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Aesthetics are secondary to feasibility. We need to be realistic about whether the proposed plans can actually be delivered on time and within the city's operational capacity.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Mio,,"I'm totally on board! But we also have to think about the future. It's not just about building it, but how much it'll cost to keep it beautiful once the party's over, right?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I agree with Mio. The initial construction is only the first step. We must determine who will actually manage the daily operations and whether the city has the manpower to sustain the park long-term.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree with all of you. However, we must also consider the physical reality of the site. A plan is only successful if it aligns with how the land drains and how people actually move through it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A very pragmatic start. Since we are all in agreement on the necessity of realism, perhaps we should examine the actual track record of our previous projects to avoid repeating past mistakes. Logic suggests the past is our best guide.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Misaki,,That makes sense. I'm particularly concerned about the actual capacity of local firms and the unpredictability of the ground here. We should look into the tendering and the phasing notes to see if the timelines are realistic.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Mio,,"That sounds like a plan! But while we're looking at the build, I really want to know about the money side. I'm curious about the upkeep costs and if there's any special funding we can use!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"To ensure the park is sustainable, we need to know the current staffing levels. I want to see the groundskeeping roll and the list of volunteer groups to see if we have enough people to actually run the place.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Minako,,I believe we need hard data on the site's behavior. I will look into the timed counts of weekday crossings and the drainage callouts and August heat readings to understand the actual usage and environmental stress.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have a comprehensive list of priorities. To complement your focus on current operations and site data, I shall investigate the condition of works from the earlier programme and the record of the eastern avenue planting.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Misaki,,I will focus on the regional firms tendering for earth-moving and the depot phasing notes on hoarding the site. It is essential to know if the contractors can actually meet the deadlines.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Mio,,I'll go with the upkeep ledger spend per hectare and the terms of the regional habitat fund! I want to see exactly where the money goes and if we have extra help!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"I will stick with my previous mentions. I'll look into the groundskeeping roll and bought-in services, as well as the volunteer groups working with the division, to assess our actual human resource capacity.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Minako,,I will proceed with my plan. I'll examine the timed counts of weekday crossings and the drainage callouts and August heat readings to ensure the chosen plan respects the site's physical and human flow.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we have a most efficient division of labor. By examining the ghosts of projects past alongside your current data, we should be able to discern which plan is a genuine vision and which is merely a mirage.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Once we have the data on contractor capacity and site phasing, we can determine which plans are actually achievable and which are simply optimistic. I look forward to seeing what we all find.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Mio,,I'm so excited to see what we find! Let's make sure we pick a plan that doesn't break the bank in a few years. I'll be waiting for everyone's reports!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. Data on staffing and volunteers will be the deciding factor for me. If we lack the personnel to maintain the site, even the most beautiful plan will eventually fail. I look forward to the results.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Minako,,"I agree. We have a solid plan to cover the financial, operational, and physical aspects of the park. I will focus on the data to ensure our final choice is grounded in reality.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
