35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems my suspicions were well-founded. While some structural work holds, our planting records are a tragedy; half the eastern avenue trees perished simply because watering was forgotten in the contract. A most elegant way to waste a budget.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"My findings are equally concerning. Only two regional firms are tendering for earth-moving, and both have flagged clay subsoil and slippage risks. This suggests that any ambitious digging could lead to significant delays and cost overruns.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh wow, this is tricky! I found out that planted areas cost three times more to maintain than hard surfaces, and that cost is actually growing every year! We have to be really careful about how much greenery we add.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The staffing situation is critical. The groundskeeping roll has plummeted from eighteen posts to just seven. We are relying heavily on bought-in services, and our existing volunteers are already fully committed to other tasks.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The site is under more stress than we imagined. Drainage callouts have doubled since the culvert was capped, and heat readings are dangerously high. Furthermore, users are ignoring margins to stick to firm ground for the tram.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, @Asuka, it seems we are facing a perfect storm of incompetence and attrition. If we cannot even remember to water trees or retain staff, a high-maintenance ""green paradise"" will simply become a graveyard of expensive saplings.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, exactly. With only two firms willing to dig and both warning about clay slippage, any plan requiring extensive earth-moving is a risk. We cannot afford delays or structural failures given our limited contractor options.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, @Asuka, you're right! And it's not just the work—it's the money! If planted areas are three times more expensive to keep up, we can't just plant everything and hope for the best. We'll be broke in no time!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, exactly. With only seven staff members left, we cannot manage a complex landscape. We must prioritize low-maintenance designs; otherwise, the burden on the remaining staff will be unsustainable and the park will deteriorate.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, @Mio, I agree. We must avoid designs that fight the land. The drainage issues and heat stress mean we need a plan that manages water effectively and provides real shade without requiring constant, intensive care.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is quite sobering, isn't it? We are essentially choosing between a plan that acknowledges our systemic failures and one that pretends they don't exist. I suspect any proposal boasting ""lush vistas"" is merely a blueprint for future decay.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. We must be wary of ""lush vistas"" if they require deep excavation in clay soil. If the ground slips or the few available firms struggle, the project will stall indefinitely. We need a plan that is physically achievable.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"But wait! There's a catch with the money! The habitat fund only pays for planting and water stuff, not buildings or paths. If we go too simple with hard surfaces, we might lose that funding entirely!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, we cannot prioritize funding over feasibility. If we take the money but have no staff to maintain the plants, we are simply paying for a future eyesore. We must choose a plan that fits our actual manpower.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, while funding is important, we cannot ignore the users. People are already avoiding soft margins to reach the tram. If we prioritize funding over firm, functional paths and drainage, we are designing a park that people cannot actually use.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have reached a consensus of caution. We must reject any plan that relies on a fantasy of infinite staffing or stable soil. Let us seek the proposal that is most honest about our limitations.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. We need a plan that minimizes deep excavation to avoid the risks of clay slippage and doesn't overextend our few remaining contractors. Practicality and a realistic timeline must be our primary criteria.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I agree! We need a balance. We can't ignore the habitat fund, but we absolutely can't afford a maintenance nightmare. Let's find a plan that's smart with the money and easy on the staff!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Exactly. We must be honest about our capacity. With the roll reduced to seven people and volunteers already stretched thin, any plan requiring intensive manual upkeep is a failure in the making. Simplicity is our only sustainable option.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I agree. We must prioritize a design that integrates functional drainage and durable paths for the tram commuters, while ensuring the greenery is sustainable given our heat stress and staffing shortages. Let us evaluate the candidates with these realities in mind.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
