60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Looking at these options, the Woodland Walk and Wetland Restoration are essentially invitations to repeat the eastern avenue tragedy. Dense planting and reshaped drainage require the very maintenance and excavation we cannot sustain.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. Wetland Restoration is particularly dangerous; reshaping drainage in clay soil with only two available firms is a recipe for slippage and endless delays. It is far too risky.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, @Misaki, you're right about the risks! But wait, the habitat fund only pays for things like the Woodland Walk or Wetland Restoration. If we pick the Plaza or Sports Terraces, where does the money come from?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, we cannot let the availability of a fund dictate a plan that we cannot maintain. Woodland Walk and Wetland Restoration require intensive care that seven staff members simply cannot provide. We must prioritize operational reality over funding.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, we must be practical. The Woodland Walk and Wetland Restoration ignore the heat stress and drainage failures we've seen. Moreover, they don't address the tram commuters who need firm, reliable paths. We need a durable solution.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, the allure of ""free"" money is a siren song that leads to expensive ruins. If we choose a plan based on a fund we cannot maintain, we are merely subsidizing a future wasteland. Logic dictates we choose durability.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, exactly. Between the remaining options, the Sports Terraces involve significant southern excavation, which is risky given the clay. The Market Plaza is the most feasible; it minimizes deep digging and relies on hard surfaces.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, I see your point! The Market Plaza is definitely the safest for the budget and the staff. It's a bit sad to lose the habitat fund, but it's better than going broke later!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Misaki, I agree. The Market Plaza is the only logical choice. It requires the least amount of ongoing manual labor, which is essential given our depleted staff and the fact that our volunteers are already fully committed.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Misaki, @Asuka, I agree. The Market Plaza provides the firm ground commuters need and avoids the drainage risks of the other plans. It is the only option that respects both the land's behavior and our limited resources.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure to see such swift alignment. We have collectively decided that a paved plaza is preferable to a lush graveyard. I shall cast my vote for the Market Plaza.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Given the clay subsoil risks and the limited number of capable firms, the Market Plaza is the only option that ensures we can actually finish the project on time. I vote for the Market Plaza.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm with you all! It's a bummer to miss out on that habitat fund, but I can't support a plan that'll bankrupt us in three years. Let's go with the Market Plaza! I vote for the Market Plaza.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree. Any other choice would be an irresponsible burden on our remaining seven staff members. We must choose the only sustainable path. I vote for the Market Plaza.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,I agree. The Market Plaza is the only plan that acknowledges the physical reality of the site and the needs of its users. It is the most sustainable choice. I vote for the Market Plaza.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a most rational conclusion. By choosing the Market Plaza, we prioritize a legacy of longevity over a fleeting, fragile beauty. A unanimous decision for the sake of pragmatism.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"It is the only responsible choice. By avoiding the risks of clay slippage and contractor shortages, we ensure the city actually gets a finished park. I am satisfied with this decision.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
77,3,4,pass,Misaki,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
78,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm glad we all agree! It's way better to have a plaza that actually works than a forest we can't afford to water. I'm happy with our choice!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
79,3,4,pass,Mio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
80,3,4,pass,Asuka,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Minako,,"Our decision is grounded in the facts. By prioritizing durability and the actual movement of the people, we have selected a plan that will truly serve the community. I am satisfied.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
